s/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/447805745","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2651#issuecomment-447805745","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2651","id":447805745,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NzgwNTc0NQ==","user":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-17T11:00:09Z","updated_at":"2018-12-17T11:00:09Z","body":"Awesome, glad that's settled. On a second look, I think there's also a bug here as that unpacking's definitely an iterating context.\r\n\r\nSo for context this check was emitted on Python 2 with the Python 3 porting checker. In Python 2, `zip` returned a list, which means that a lot of operations that are invalid in Python 3 were done on the output of `zip`, such as indexing elements and such, so that's what the check is supposed to find, operations against a `zip` that is not in an iterable, materializing context. But since pylint 2.X moved to Python 3 only, we still look for these checks, if they are activated with `--py3k` as that is our signal that we are linting against a Python 2 file. But the bug here is that `*` is definitely a materializing context, so the check shouldn't apply to it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/447805745/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2029925251,"node_id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MjAyOTkyNTI1MQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/events/2029925251","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gist